[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3515927279","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112635#issuecomment-3515927279","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112635","id":3515927279,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RkMrv","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-11T09:48:45Z","updated_at":"2025-11-11T09:51:07Z","body":"This is an undocumented quirk of the class, the timer doesn't allow modifying the behavior once the timer is started, changing this would break compatibility with existing use so this should probably be properly documented instead \n\nThe timer is started *before* `_ready` is called so the timer uses the value set on the node before, and ignores the value from `_ready`, you should use `timer.start(100)` instead to achieve the desired result ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3515927279/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3516074290","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112635#issuecomment-3516074290","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112635","id":3516074290,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Rkwky","user":{"login":"skincrawl","id":123931483,"node_id":"U_kgDOB2MLWw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123931483?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl","html_url":"https://github.com/skincrawl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-11T10:17:31Z","updated_at":"2025-11-11T10:18:12Z","body":"> This is an undocumented quirk of the class, the timer doesn't allow modifying the behavior once the timer is started, changing this would break compatibility with existing use so this should probably be properly documented instead\n> \n> The timer is started _before_ `_ready` is called so the timer uses the value set on the node before, and ignores the value from `_ready`, you should use `timer.start(100)` instead to achieve the desired result\n\nThank you for replying!\nOhh I see. That explains it. Would be more clear if it gave a warning or something when changing wait time after the fact. And yeah, I also didn't realize it had already been started at _ready(). :p","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3516074290/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3516110175","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112635#issuecomment-3516110175","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112635","id":3516110175,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Rk5Vf","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-11T10:22:52Z","updated_at":"2025-11-11T10:28:35Z","body":"It's perfectly valid to modify it so a warning wouldn't be good\n\nYou are doing this in the `_ready` of the *parent* of the timer, which means the timer is fully done being ready, so this is expected, though I'm not sure if running the code in the `_ready` of the timer itself would change anything, I don't remember if the notification or the method are fired first (a timer that has auto start on starts itself in the ready notification)\n\nBut the fact that `wait_time` is copied to `time_left` and that `time_left` is then the only thing affecting the way the timer behaves after you start it should be explained, it's hinted at but not stated explicitly","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3516110175/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3516163557","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112635#issuecomment-3516163557","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112635","id":3516163557,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RlGXl","user":{"login":"skincrawl","id":123931483,"node_id":"U_kgDOB2MLWw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/123931483?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl","html_url":"https://github.com/skincrawl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skincrawl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-11T10:30:03Z","updated_at":"2025-11-11T10:30:03Z","body":"> It's perfectly valid to modify it so a warning wouldn't be good\n> \n> You are doing this in the `_ready` of the _parent_ of the timer, which means the timer is fully done being ready, so this is expected, though I'm not sure if running the code in the `_ready` of the timer itself would change anything, I don't remember if the notification or the method are fired first (a timer that has auto start on starts itself in the ready notification)\n\nOh yeah, well I guess adding it in the documentation would be good then.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3516163557/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527099506","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112635#issuecomment-3527099506","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112635","id":3527099506,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SO0Ry","user":{"login":"inkusgames","id":142333117,"node_id":"U_kgDOCHvUvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142333117?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/inkusgames","html_url":"https://github.com/inkusgames","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inkusgames/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inkusgames/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inkusgames/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inkusgames/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inkusgames/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inkusgames/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inkusgames/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inkusgames/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/inkusgames/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T10:34:19Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T10:42:41Z","body":"> It's perfectly valid to modify it so a warning wouldn't be good\n\nCould we not give a warning only if the timer has already started.\n\n``` cpp\n\nvoid Timer::set_wait_time(double p_time) {\n\tERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(p_time <= 0, \"Time should be greater than zero.\");\n\tERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(time_left >= 0, \"The wait time can not be changed on a running timer.\");\n\twait_time = p_time;\n\tupdate_configuration_warnings();\n}\n\n```\n_Small edits done to to code suggestion._","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527099506/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527154620","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112635#issuecomment-3527154620","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112635","id":3527154620,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SPBu8","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"htt